Aerie-Purpose: Remove Helium's services page, its Settings row and route, and the spell check message that tells users to enable Helium services; keep the extension proxy address as one row on the privacy page.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (privacy_page, route, router, lazy_load, BUILD.gn); chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_localized_strings_provider.cc; chrome/app/generated_resources.grd; chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages.cc; chrome/browser/download/download_ui_model.cc
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #23. Helium services are off (services/0002), so the page's toggles for bangs, spell
check files, uBlock Origin assets and browser updates do nothing, its "setup pending" notice
never goes away, and its crash reporting menu does nothing (crash/0001). The page, the
settings-helium-services-page element, the route (chrome://settings/privacy/services) and
the changelog proxy go. The two places that opened that route (ShowHeliumServices and the
download bubble's "enable Helium services" link) open the privacy page instead, and a saved
link to the old path falls back to the Settings home page.

The one control that still works, the extension proxy address, becomes a row of the privacy
page that reads and writes the same pref (helium.services.origin_override). The browser
validates the value again (aerie services validator, https only), so the pattern on the input
only stops a bad address from being sent. The pattern is written for Chrome's v flag, where a
"/" inside [...] must be escaped; in the .html file the backslash is doubled because the
generated wrapper puts the markup in a template literal (tests/test_extension_proxy_row.py
compiles it). Its strings and the spell check note are Aerie messages in
chrome/app/aerie_services_strings.grdp (overlay), included from generated_resources.grd. The
C++ plumbing of the services (prefs, handlers, strings that no page uses any more) stays, to
keep Helium bumps cheap.

Depends on the Helium patches services-prefs.patch, onboarding-page.patch,
reenable-spellcheck-downloads.patch and add-updater-preference.patch (they add the files and
strings this patch removes or replaces) and on hardening/0003 and onboarding/0001.

